# Normalize line endings repo-wide: git stores LF; Windows working tree gets CRLF via core.autocrlf.
# Added 2026-07-12 to end perpetual phantom-modified flags from pre-existing CRLF blobs.
* text=auto

# .claude/hooks/session-start.sh is invoked as a bare path by settings.json (relies on the
# shebang, not an explicit interpreter) and does real work in the remote/web Linux environment
# this hook targets -- a CRLF-corrupted "#!/bin/bash\r" shebang there is a live "bad interpreter"
# risk (harmless locally only because the script no-ops unless CLAUDE_CODE_REMOTE=true). Force LF
# regardless of platform checkout, matching ora-skills' tools/hooks/* precedent. bash-guard.mjs and
# file-guard.mjs are NOT included here -- both are invoked with an explicit `node` prefix in
# settings.json, so their shebang (and therefore CRLF-vs-LF) is irrelevant; scoping this narrowly
# to the one file with an actual exposure, not the whole hooks/ directory.
.claude/hooks/session-start.sh text eol=lf
